# ConstitutionCourt — line-ending normalization
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS AT COMMIT 1, NOT LATER
#
# GenLayer derives a contract's address from the transaction that carries its
# source bytes. The deploy payload is the file, byte for byte — there is no
# compilation step to normalize it away. So the checkout's line endings are
# part of the deployed artifact's identity.
#
# On a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true, git materializes CRLF. On
# Linux CI it materializes LF. Same commit, two different byte strings, two
# different sha256 digests, two different contract addresses. App 1
# (GIFTEDLOV/uptimebond) hit exactly this: a bundle built on Windows and one
# built on Linux CI deployed *different contracts* from the same commit, and
# it was only caught because a reproducibility check hashed the file on both.
#
# Pinning to LF makes the deployed bytes a property of the commit rather than
# a property of whoever built it. This is cheap to do now and expensive to
# retrofit after addresses have been published.

# --- Contract sources: consensus-critical, LF is mandatory ------------------
contracts/**/*.py                 text eol=lf
frontend/src/contract/*.py        text eol=lf

# --- Evidence fixtures: fetched by validators over HTTPS --------------------
# Not hashed on-chain, but validators re-fetch and re-derive from these. Stable
# bytes keep diffs honest and keep fixture-served content identical across
# platforms.
evidence/**/*.json                text eol=lf
evidence/**/*.md                  text eol=lf

# --- Everything else --------------------------------------------------------
*.py       text eol=lf
*.md       text eol=lf
*.json     text eol=lf
*.yml      text eol=lf
*.yaml     text eol=lf
*.txt      text eol=lf
*.ts       text eol=lf
*.tsx      text eol=lf
*.js       text eol=lf
*.mjs      text eol=lf
*.cjs      text eol=lf
*.css      text eol=lf
*.html     text eol=lf
*.ini      text eol=lf
.gitignore      text eol=lf
.gitattributes  text eol=lf

# --- Binary: never touch ----------------------------------------------------
*.png      binary
*.jpg      binary
*.jpeg     binary
*.gif      binary
*.webp     binary
*.ico      binary
*.woff     binary
*.woff2    binary
*.pdf      binary
